{"Id":"CHECK_0128","Area":"Services","AuditCheck":"'Print Spooler (Spooler)' is set to 'Disabled'","Expected":"Startup type Disabled (Start = 4), or service not installed","Steps":"On {HOST}, open Services (services.msc). Open the properties of Print Spooler (service name: Spooler). Check that Startup type is Disabled; close with Cancel. If the service is not listed, it is not installed and the check is met.\n\nEquivalent GP UI path:\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Windows Settings\\Security Settings\\System Services\\Print Spooler\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Spooler\nValue name: Start\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 4 (decimal; 0x00000004)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. If the service key does not exist, the service is not installed.","CheckType":"GUI and registry verification","Rationale":"Cyberfort recommends disabling unneeded Print Spooler services to reduce exposure to PrintNightmare and other attacks against printing services.","Impact":"Printing and print sharing, including PDF printing dependent on Spooler, will stop; review application and printing requirements before disabling."},
{"Id":"CHECK_0129","Area":"Services","AuditCheck":"'Problem Reports and Solutions Control Panel Support (wercplsupport)' is set to 'Disabled'","Expected":"Startup type Disabled (Start = 4), or service not installed","Steps":"On {HOST}, open Services (services.msc). Open the properties of Problem Reports and Solutions Control Panel Support (service name: wercplsupport). Check that Startup type is Disabled; close with Cancel. If the service is not listed, it is not installed and the check is met.\n\nEquivalent GP UI path:\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Windows Settings\\Security Settings\\System Services\\Problem Reports and Solutions Control Panel Support\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\wercplsupport\nValue name: Start\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 4 (decimal; 0x00000004)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. If the service key does not exist, the service is not installed.","CheckType":"GUI and registry verification","Rationale":"Cyberfort recommends disabling the Problem Reports and Solutions Control Panel Support service on workstations that do not need it, to limit the submission of error report data to Microsoft.","Impact":"Viewing and sending system-level problem reports from the Security and Maintenance control panel will not work."},
{"Id":"CHECK_0130","Area":"Services","AuditCheck":"'Remote Access Auto Connection Manager (RasAuto)' is set to 'Disabled'","Expected":"Startup type Disabled (Start = 4), or service not installed","Steps":"On {HOST}, open Services (services.msc). Open the properties of Remote Access Auto Connection Manager (service name: RasAuto). Check that Startup type is Disabled; close with Cancel. If the service is not listed, it is not installed and the check is met.\n\nEquivalent GP UI path:\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Windows Settings\\Security Settings\\System Services\\Remote Access Auto Connection Manager\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\RasAuto\nValue name: Start\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 4 (decimal; 0x00000004)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. If the service key does not exist, the service is not installed.","CheckType":"GUI and registry verification","Rationale":"Cyberfort recommends disabling the Remote Access Auto Connection Manager service on workstations that do not need it, to prevent the device from automatically dialling out to remote networks.","Impact":"Dial-up and some VPN connections will not start automatically when a remote name or address is referenced."},
