{"Id":"CHECK_0133","Area":"Services","AuditCheck":"'Remote Desktop Services UserMode Port Redirector (UmRdpService)' is set to 'Disabled'","Expected":"Startup type Disabled (Start = 4), or service not installed","Steps":"On {HOST}, open Services (services.msc). Open the properties of Remote Desktop Services UserMode Port Redirector (service name: UmRdpService). Check that Startup type is Disabled; close with Cancel. If the service is not listed, it is not installed and the check is met.\n\nEquivalent GP UI path:\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Windows Settings\\Security Settings\\System Services\\Remote Desktop Services UserMode Port Redirector\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\UmRdpService\nValue name: Start\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 4 (decimal; 0x00000004)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. If the service key does not exist, the service is not installed.","CheckType":"GUI and registry verification","Rationale":"Cyberfort recommends disabling the Remote Desktop Services UserMode Port Redirector service on workstations that do not need it, to prevent drive, printer and port redirection in Remote Desktop sessions.","Impact":"Device redirection in inbound Remote Desktop sessions will not work."},
