{"Id":"CHECK_0268","Area":"Administrative templates","AuditCheck":"'Configure RPC packet level privacy setting for incoming connections' is set to 'Enabled'","Expected":"Equals: 1","Steps":{"Workgroup":"On {HOST}, open Local Group Policy Editor (gpedit.msc). Navigate to:\n\nComputer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\MS Security Guide\\Configure RPC packet level privacy setting for incoming connections\n\nCheck that 'Configure RPC packet level privacy setting for incoming connections' is set to Enabled.\n\nGP UI path:\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Administrative Templates\\MS Security Guide\\Configure RPC packet level privacy setting for incoming connections\n\nRead the displayed setting.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Print\nValue name: RpcAuthnLevelPrivacyEnabled\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 1 (decimal; 0x00000001)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. A missing value remains unresolved unless the check explicitly requires absence.","Shared":"Open Group Policy Management (gpmc.msc) on an administrative computer. Right-click Group Policy Results and start Group Policy Results Wizard. Select {HOST} as the target computer, complete the wizard, and open the Settings tab. Inspect the applied setting at:\n\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Administrative Templates\\MS Security Guide\\Configure RPC packet level privacy setting for incoming connections\n\nCheck that 'Configure RPC packet level privacy setting for incoming connections' is set to Enabled.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Print\nValue name: RpcAuthnLevelPrivacyEnabled\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 1 (decimal; 0x00000001)\n\