{"Id":"CHECK_0373","Area":"BitLocker profile (BL)","AuditCheck":"'Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Omit recovery options from the BitLocker setup wizard' is set to 'Enabled: True'","Expected":"Equals: 1","Steps":{"Workgroup":"On {HOST}, open Local Group Policy Editor (gpedit.msc). Navigate to:\n\nComputer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Omit recovery options from the BitLocker setup wizard\n\nCheck that 'Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Omit recovery options from the BitLocker setup wizard' is set to Enabled: True.\n\nGP UI path:\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Omit recovery options from the BitLocker setup wizard\n\nRead the displayed setting.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\nValue name: FDVHideRecoveryPage\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 1 (decimal; 0x00000001)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. A missing value remains unresolved unless the check explicitly requires absence.","Shared":"Open Group Policy Management (gpmc.msc) on an administrative computer. Right-click Group Policy Results and start Group Policy Results Wizard. Select {HOST} as the target computer, complete the wizard, and open the Settings tab. Inspect the applied setting at:\n\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Omit recovery options from the BitLocker setup wizard\n\nCheck that 'Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Omit recovery options from the BitLocker setup wizard' is set to Enabled: True.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\nValue name: FDVHideRecoveryPage\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 1 (decimal; 0x00000001)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. A missing value remains unresolved unless the check explicitly requires absence."},"CheckType":"GUI and registry verification","Rationale":"Cyberfort recommends defining how BitLocker-protected fixed data drives are recovered, so that data remains recoverable by the organisation without leaving weak or unmanaged recovery methods available.","Impact":"Users cannot choose recovery options when turning on BitLocker for a fixed data drive; the policy determines them."},
{"Id":"CHECK_0374","Area":"BitLocker profile (BL)","AuditCheck":"'Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Save BitLocker recovery information to AD DS for fixed data drives' is set to 'Enabled: False'","Expected":"Equals: 0","Steps":{"Workgroup":"On {HOST}, open Local Group Policy Editor (gpedit.msc). Navigate to:\n\nComputer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Save BitLocker recovery information to AD DS for fixed data drives\n\nCheck that 'Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Save BitLocker recovery information to AD DS for fixed data drives' is set to Enabled: False.\n\nGP UI path:\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Save BitLocker recovery information to AD DS for fixed data drives\n\nRead the displayed setting.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\nValue name: FDVActiveDirectoryBackup\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 0 (decimal; 0x00000000)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. A missing value remains unresolved unless the check explicitly requires absence.","Shared":"Open Group Policy Management (gpmc.msc) on an administrative computer. Right-click Group Policy Results and start Group Policy Results Wizard. Select {HOST} as the target computer, complete the wizard, and open the Settings tab. Inspect the applied setting at:\n\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Save BitLocker recovery information to