an be recovered: Configure storage of BitLocker recovery information to AD DS\n\nCheck that 'Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Configure storage of BitLocker recovery information to AD DS' is set to Enabled: Backup recovery passwords and key packages.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\nValue name: FDVActiveDirectoryInfoToStore\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 1 (decimal; 0x00000001)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. A missing value remains unresolved unless the check explicitly requires absence."},"CheckType":"GUI and registry verification","Rationale":"Cyberfort recommends defining how BitLocker-protected fixed data drives are recovered, so that data remains recoverable by the organisation without leaving weak or unmanaged recovery methods available.","Impact":"If AD DS backup is later enabled, both recovery passwords and key packages are stored."},
