rives\\Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Do not enable BitLocker until recovery information is stored to AD DS for fixed data drives\n\nCheck that 'Choose how BitLocker-protected fixed drives can be recovered: Do not enable BitLocker until recovery information is stored to AD DS for fixed data drives' is set to Enabled: False.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\nValue name: FDVRequireActiveDirectoryBackup\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 0 (decimal; 0x00000000)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. A missing value remains unresolved unless the check explicitly requires absence."},"CheckType":"GUI and registry verification","Rationale":"Cyberfort recommends defining how BitLocker-protected fixed data drives are recovered, so that data remains recoverable by the organisation without leaving weak or unmanaged recovery methods available.","Impact":"BitLocker can be turned on for fixed data drives without first backing up recovery information to AD DS."},
{"Id":"CHECK_0377","Area":"BitLocker profile (BL)","AuditCheck":"'Configure use of hardware-based encryption for fixed data drives' is set to 'Disabled'","Expected":"Equals: 0","Steps":{"Workgroup":"On {HOST}, open Local Group Policy Editor (gpedit.msc). Navigate to:\n\nComputer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Configure use of hardware-based encryption for fixed data drives\n\nCheck that 'Configure use of hardware-based encryption for fixed data drives' is set to Disabled.\n\nGP UI path:\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Configure use of hardware-based encryption for fixed data drives\n\nRead the displayed setting.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\nValue name: FDVHardwareEncryption\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 0 (decimal; 0x00000000)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. A missing value remains unresolved unless the check explicitly requires absence.","Shared":"Open Group Policy Management (gpmc.msc) on an administrative computer. Right-click Group Policy Results and start Group Policy Results Wizard. Select {HOST} as the target computer, complete the wizard, and open the Settings tab. Inspect the applied setting at:\n\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Configure use of hardware-based encryption for fixed data drives\n\nCheck that 'Configure use of hardware-based encryption for fixed data drives' is set to Disabled.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\nValue name: FDVHardwareEncryption\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 0 (decimal; 0x00000000)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. A missing value remains unresolved unless the check explicitly requires absence."},"CheckType":"GUI and registry verification","Rationale":"Cyberfort recommends software-based BitLocker encryption for fixed data drives, because drive firmware encryption has had vulnerabilities that allow protection to be bypassed.","Impact":"BitLocker always uses software-based encryption; there may be a small performance cost on drives that support hardware encryption."},
{"Id":"CHECK_0378","Area":"BitLocker profile (BL)","AuditCheck":"'Configure use of passwords for fixed data drives' is set to 'Disabled'","Expected":"Equals: 0","Steps":{"Workgroup":"On {HOST}, open Local Group Policy Editor (gpedit.msc). Navigate to:\n\nComputer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Configure use of passwords for fixed data drives\n\nCheck that 'Configure use of passwords for fixed data drives' is set to Disabled.\n\nGP UI path:\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Configure use of passwords for fixed data drives\n\nRead the displayed setting.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\nValue name: FDVPassphrase\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 0 (decimal; 0x00000000)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. A missing value remains unresolved unless the check explicitly requires absence.","Shared":"Open Group Policy Management (gpmc.msc) on an administrative computer. Right-click Group Policy Results and start Group Policy Results Wizard. Select {HOST} as the target computer, complete the wizard, and open the Settings tab. Inspect the applied setting at:\n\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Configure use of passwords for fixed data drives\n\nCheck that 'Configure use of passwords for fixed data drives' is set to Disabled.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\nValue name: FDVPassphrase\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 0 (decimal; 0x00000000)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. A missing value remains unresolved unless the check explicitly requires absence."},"CheckType":"GUI and registry verification","Rationale":"Cyberfort recommends that passwords are not used to unlock BitLocker-protected fixed data drives, because passwords are easier to guess or capture than certificate or TPM-based protectors.","Impact":"Fixed data drives cannot be unlocked with a password; automatic unlock or smart cards must be used."},
{"Id":"CHECK_0379","Area":"BitLocker profile (BL)","AuditCheck":"'Configure use of smart cards on fixed data drives' is set to 'Enabled'","Expected":"Equals: 1","Steps":{"Workgroup":"On {HOST}, open Local Group Policy Editor (gpedit.msc). Navigate to:\n\nComputer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Configure use of smart cards on fixed data drives\n\nCheck that 'Configure use of smart cards on fixed data drives' is set to Enabled.\n\nGP UI path:\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Configure use of smart cards on fixed data drives\n\nRead the displayed setting.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\nValue name: FDVAllowUserCert\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 1 (decimal; 0x00000001)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. A missing value remains unresolved unless the check explicitly requires absence.","Shared":"Open Group Policy Management (gpmc.msc) on an administrative computer. Right-click Group Policy Results and start Group Policy Results Wizard. Select {HOST} as the target computer, complete the wizard, and open the Settings tab. Inspect the applied setting at:\n\nComputer Configuration\\Policies\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\BitLocker Drive Encryption\\Fixed Data Drives\\Configure use of smart cards on fixed data drives\n\nCheck that 'Configure use of smart cards on fixed data drives' is set to Enabled.\n\nRegistry verification on {HOST}:\nOpen Registry Editor (regedit.exe) and read the following existing values in the 64-bit registry view:\n\nKey: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\nValue name: FDVAllowUserCert\nExpected type: REG_DWORD\nExpected data: 1 (decimal; 0x00000001)\n\nRead the type and data without changing them. A missing value remains unresolved unless the check explicitly requires absence."},"CheckType":"GUI and registry verification","Rationale":"Cyberfort recommends smart card protection for BitLocker-protected fixed data drives, so that unlocking the drive requires a physical token and its PIN.","Impact":"A smart card with a suitable certificate is needed to protect and unlock the drive; smart card infrastructure must be in place."},
